    "created_at": "2017-08-15T14:13:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-15T14:24:58Z",
    "body": "@domenic This is a specification issue. There's no way for an automated tool to determine the correct merge order of atomized ruby text without a modification to HTML as far as I can tell.\r\n\r\nThe example was showing why I think an `rt` element attribute is an ideal solution for encoding that information. Another solution that's less verbose might be something like `<ruby merge-order=\"reverse\">`.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
