    "updated_at": "2017-08-15T14:37:24Z",
    "body": "@domenic Actually, `merge-order=\"reverse\"` works in some cases (e.g., two-ideographic-character names or where one has atomized the aforementioned name into two ruby texts instead of three), but not this case. Position numbers will still be required to encode this information (e.g., `merge-order=\"3 1 2\"`).",
